When a buffer can't be imported (out of GPU memory), commit posts an
error and returns after taking down the pending state's handler for the
buffer's destruction but without taking the reference the state then
owns. Clearing the state later unrefs a buffer it holds no reference to,
freeing the MetaWaylandBuffer while it still listens for its wl_buffer's
destruction, and GNOME Shell crashes (in wl_list_remove) when the client
is destroyed for the error. Drop the pointer instead.

--- a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-surface.c
+++ b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-surface.c
@@ -1157,6 +1157,9 @@ meta_wayland_surface_commit (MetaWaylandSurface *surface)
                                   "Failed to attach buffer to surface %i: %s",
                                   wl_resource_get_id (surface->resource),
                                   error->message);
+          /* Without its destroy handler the state would own the buffer
+           * and unref it when cleared, but it has taken no reference. */
+          pending->buffer = NULL;
           return;
         }
 
